* ============================================================================
*  Flyback / free-wheeling diode  (1N4148-class small signal, or a Schottky)
* ============================================================================
*  Written as a sub-circuit so the terminal order is spelled out explicitly:
*  KiCad's diode symbol pin 1 is the cathode (K) and pin 2 is the anode (A),
*  and this sub-circuit keeps that mapping unambiguous for ngspice.
*
*      anode  -> current flows A -> K inside the model
*      cathode (K) sits on the +12 V rail, anode on the switching node
*
*  KiCad reads this file through the D1 "Sim.Library" / "Sim.Name" fields.
* ============================================================================
.subckt diode_fast K A
Dint A K diode_fast_model
.model diode_fast_model d(is=2.2p rs=0.6 cjo=4p tt=11.5n bv=75 ibv=100u)
.ends
